    "blind_description": "This is a line drawing of a corner storefront in three-quarter perspective:\n- Upper element: two rectangular signboards meeting at the building corner, each bearing handwritten legible text **CAFÉ**. Thin straight connector lines descend from each sign's corners/edge to the awning below.\n- Awning: a long rectangular valence wraps the corner, segmented by short vertical lines, with a continuous wavy scalloped lower edge. Small open triangular gusset lines connect its outer ends to the wall.\n- Facade: two angled walls meet at the corner. On each side of the central double door is a large four-pane window (one vertical and one horizontal mullion each). The central closed double door has two tall vertical inset panels and two short vertical handles; the door outline and its threshold are complete.\n- Foreground: two simple pedestal tables, each made of an oval top, a single vertical stem, and an oval base; no chairs are shown.\nAll drawn contours are complete; no people, interior contents, or additional attached objects are depicted.",
